** FFXtreme Release Notes
** Frank Beentjes <frankbeen@gmail.com>
************************************

** v2.0 - october 2026
 - Upgrading: the OSD settings are reset to factory defaults on first
   start (the configuration layout changed).
 - Fixed: OSD jumped vertically on the Atari ST. The HSYNC interrupt
   now samples VSYNC itself, instead of racing a separate VSYNC interrupt.
 - New: separate vertical offset for 60 Hz colour ("60Hz V.Off").
 - New: clean restart when switching between colour and monochrome.
 - Keyboard: received by interrupt into a buffer (no lost bytes); mouse
   and joystick packets are skipped, so they cannot trigger hotkeys;
   keys no longer get stuck; hotkeys need both Ctrl and Alt.
 - Keyboard: recovers cleanly if bytes are lost (buffer overflow).
 - TOS (Ctrl+Alt+F1-F4), boot drive (Ctrl+Alt+B) and sound (Ctrl+Alt+S)
   are saved, so they survive a power cycle (EmuTOS needs a cold start).
 - Ctrl+Alt+Delete resets the Atari ST instead of the OSD controller.
 - OSD menu: Ctrl+Alt+Undo leaves it without saving; it closes by
   itself after one minute without key presses.
 - Fixed: every settings save restarted the OSD controller (Flash write
   never terminated, the watchdog reset the chip).
 - Fixed: mono/stereo messages were swapped and could show the old state.
 - TOS and sound select lines are driven actively (were weak pulls).
 - PB8/PB9 (unused Gotek button lines) are no longer driven low.
 - Updated factory default H.Off/V.Off.
 - Builds with GCC 12 and newer.

** v1.9 - december 2022
